t\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, SOL, DOT, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The bears pressed the sell button on Bitcoin and select altcoins after U.S. inflation data came in hotter than expected.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to stay above $23,000 as the weekend approaches. The selling pressure increased after the personal consumption expenditures excluding food and energy rose 0.6% in January and 4.7% over the year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-stays-24k-as-pce-data-helps-us-dollar-near-7-week-highs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 above market expectations}}}\uc2  of an increase of 0.5% and 4.4% respectively.\par \par \uc2 This could trigger fears that the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2  may have to continue its rate hikes to bring inflation under control. Expectations of a rate hike could strengthen the U.S. dollar index further, which is already near a seven-week high, and that may put pressure on the cryptocurrency markets in the near term.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/45bc59bf-8a1c-4d96-9d13-5755fe8fe672.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 A drop in the cryptocurrency markets may start a discussion that the rally in January may have been a bull trap. However, the price action in Bitcoin and several altcoins show that a bottoming formation may have begun. The next dip may form a higher low before attempting a move higher.\par \par \uc2 What are the important support levels in Bitcoin and altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers successfully held the 20-day exponential moving average ($23,440) for the past two days but the failure to sustain the rebound attracted strong selling on Feb. 24.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/fdc97845-3f51-427a-9e4f-19a7ba0c2a6a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the relative strength index (RSI) suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is weakening. The BTC/USDT pair has reached immediate support at $22,800.\par \par \uc2 A break below this level could retest the crucial support zone between the 50-day simple moving average ($22,052) and $21,480.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price fails to sustain below the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that bulls are buying the dips as they anticipate a move higher. A break and close above $25,250 may start the next leg of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) slipped below the 20-day EMA ($1,624) on Feb. 22 but the long tail on the candlestick shows solid buying at lower levels. The bulls tried to build upon the advantage on Feb. 23 and drive the price above $1,680 but the bears held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/71e91b49-896a-47a1-b754-5cb3413a02ca.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling intensified on Feb. 24 and the price dropped to the 50-day SMA ($1,565). This is an important support for the bulls to guard because if it cracks, the ETH/USDT pair could plummet to $1,461.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the pric