ative territory, indicating that bears have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/09e47ada-4289-48fe-b2bb-aedf26a6889c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the 50-day SMA ($1,483) fails to arrest the decline, the selling could accelerate and the ETH/USDT pair may fall to the solid support at $1,352. This level may attract aggressive buying by the bulls. If the price rebounds off it, the pair may oscillate between $1,352 and $1,680 for some time.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns up from the 50-day SMA and breaks above the 20-day EMA. The pair could then rally to $1,680, which remains the key level for the bulls to surmount.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) faced rejection at $318 on Feb. 12, suggesting that bears are selling on rallies. The bears will try to strengthen their position further by dragging the price below the strong support at $280.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/2d08bd88-3f32-4e74-9f75-1dadd3711180.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($310) has started to turn down and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating that bears are at an advantage. If the $280 level collapses, the BNB/USDT pair may witness aggressive selling. The next support is $250.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price jumps up from $280, the bulls will again try to push the pair above $318. If they succeed, the pair could rise to the neckline of the developing inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls failed to protect the 50-day SMA ($0.38), indicating a lack of demand at lower levels. XRP\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) next support is at $0.36.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/1b9e4c13-61c6-479c-8f8a-419ed755a652.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.39) has started to turn down and the RSI has slipped into the negative territory, indicating that bears have the edge.\par \par \uc2 Even if the price rebounds off $0.36, the bears will try to sell on rallies to the 20-day EMA. If the price turns down from this level, it will increase the likelihood of a break below $0.36. The XRP/USDT pair could then plunge to $0.33.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up and rises above the 20-day EMA, the pair may remain stuck between $0.36 and $0.43 for a while longer.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) is witnessing a tough battle between the bulls and the bears near the moving averages. A minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the price to sustain below the 50-day SMA ($0.08).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/6ac9c9b7-2600-41d0-b359-9d08e4fa4e01.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers propel the price above the 20-day EMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to the psychological resistance at $0.10. The bears are expected to protect the zone between $0.10 and $0.11 with vigor because if it is scaled, the pair could pick up momentum and skyrocket to $0.15.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price sustains below the 50-day SMA, the bears will attempt to sink the pair to the critical support at $0.07. This level is likely to attract aggressive buying by the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-flirts-with-bid-liquidity-as-btc-price-nears-new-3-week-lows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin flirts with bid liquidity as BTC price nears new 3-week lows}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to push Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) back above the 20-day EMA ($0.37) on Feb. 12 but the bears did not budge. This shows that the sellers are trying to gain the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/722abab7-ad37-40df-8100-d4742ddfac86.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears yanked the price below the immediate support at $0.35, which paves the way for a potential drop to the 50-day SMA ($0.34) and then to the crucial support at $0.32. A break below this level will suggest that bears are back in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to prevent a deep correction, they will have to quickly kick the price above the $0.38 resistance. If the price sustains above this level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could climb to $0.41 and thereafter to $0.44. This level is likely to pose a strong challenge for the bulls.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers tried to propel Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) above the $1.30 overhead resistance on Feb. 12 but the bears held their ground. This may have tempted short-term traders to book profits, which dragged the price below the 20-day EMA ($1.17).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/3e0a1b56-a581-422a-8043-cd46651d7598.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the bears sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, the MATIC/USDT pair could plummet to the 50-day SMA ($1.05). The zone between $1.05 and $1 is likely to attract buyers.\par \par \uc2 Usually, after such a deep correction, the next leg of the uptrend may not start at once. The price could oscillate between $1.30 and $1.05 for a few days before starting the next trending move.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns up from the current level and rises to the overhead resistance at $1.35.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) plunged below the 20-day EMA ($22.19) on Feb. 9 but the bears failed to pull the price below the 50-day SMA ($19.42) on Feb. 10. This shows that lower levels are attracting buyers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/c79d5335-3e3a-4adb-95f3-bff5083fd4c2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down from the 20-day EMA on Feb. 13, indicating that bears are trying to establish their supremacy. If the price slides below the 50-day SMA, the selling could pick up and the SOL/USDT pair may collapse to $15.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the overhead resistance at $28. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break above it will signal a potential trend change.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the authors\u8217\'20\'19 alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvNzA1YjM2NTgtNmUyYy00YmYxLTg5ZGMtOGZlOTI5NmY0MjNiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230213ej2d000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/10: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, DOT, LTC, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,769 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The crypto market corrected as the SEC announced that staking as a service programs are illegal, and this has traders worried that regulators will turn the screw even further.\par \par \uc2 On Feb. 9, \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) chair \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2  explained why the regulator had cracked down on Kraken cryptocurrency exchange, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/kraken-reaches-30m-settlement-with-sec-over-staking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forcing it to stop its crypto staking program}}}\uc2  for U.S. clients. This news may have rattled crypto investors and they sold aggressively. Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-taps-3-week-lows-as-sec-fears-liquidate-250m-of-crypto-longs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed about 5%}}}\uc2  on Feb. 9 and several altcoins also followed suit.\par \par \uc2 The fresh round of selling has traders wondering whether the bear market has resumed or if the dip should be interpreted as a buying opportunity. This question may be troubling to investors, but for now the correction looks to be a normal corrective phase where cryptocurrencies give back some of the gains made in January. However, it would be prudent to wait for the correction to end and a bottom to be confirmed before considering fresh purchases.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/564ff4da-057b-4829-8ed3-a7d4aeb1b950.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Former BitMEX CEO Arthur Hayes said in a Feb. 7 blog post that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/arthur-hayes-bets-on-bitcoin-altcoin-surge-in-h1-2023-as-he-buys-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin may continue its bull run}}}\uc2  in the first half of the year but may face challenges in the latter half. Along with Bitcoin and Ether, Hayes is also \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on altcoins but he said the trick is to get the timing right.\par \par \uc2 What are the important support levels to watch out for Bitcoin and altcoins in the near term? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The $22,800 support cracked on Feb. 9 and Bitcoin plunged to the strong support near $21,480. A lack of a strong bounce off this level suggests that the correction may deepen further.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/0b4d06ff-297e-4f62-99cb-31d4e4f1c00c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Below $21,480, the selling could accelerate and the BTC/USDT pair could fall to the moving averages. The relative strength index (RSI) has slipped into the negative territory, indicating that bears are trying to gain the upper hand in the near term.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a golden cross but the bulls need to flip the 200-day simple moving average ($19,722) into support if they want to remain in the game.\par \par \uc2 A strong rebound off the zone between $21,480 and the 200-day SMA will suggest that bulls are trying to form a higher low. The pair could then gradually move back toward $24,255. The bulls will have to surmount the $25,211 resistance to suggest that the downtrend is over.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears did not allow Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) to sustain above the $1,680 level which may have tempted short-term bulls to book profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/0a1b015c-2db9-4021-ba94-e5b269f12cc2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a golden cross, indicating a potential trend change but the bears are unlikely to give up without a fight. The sellers will try to pull the price below the moving averages and trap the aggressive bulls. If they can pull it off, the selling could intensify and a collapse to $1,200 is possible.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns up from the moving averages, it will indicate that bulls are trying to flip the 200-day SMA ($1,442) into support. The bulls will then make another attempt to thrust the price above $1,680 and gain control. The ETH/USDT pair could then start its northward march toward $2,000.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) nose-dived back below the breakout level of $318 on Feb. 9, which shows aggressive selling at higher levels. This clears the path for a possible dump to the 200-day SMA ($287).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/4f4105ec-7256-4da1-a467-4dd28e6d1914.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are likely to defend the moving averages with vigor. If the price rebounds off this support with force, the BNB/USDT pair could form an inverse head and shoulders pattern, which will complete on a break and close above the neckline. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal setup has a target objective of $440.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price breaks below the moving averages, the selling could intensify and the pair may tumble to $240.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 After staying above the 200-day SMA ($0.39) for several days, XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) plummeted below the support on Feb. 9. This suggests that bears are trying to take charge.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/cea1dcfe-f216-4e92-9cda-8b61d0056c91.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 50-day SMA ($0.38) had acted as a strong support on Jan. 18 and the bulls are again trying to protect the level. If the price jumps up from the current level and rises above the 200-day SMA, it will hint at strong demand at lower levels. The buyers will then aim to overcome the barrier at $0.43 and start an up-move toward $0.51.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the 50-day SMA gives way, it will signal that bears are back in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat. The XRP/USDT pair could then drop to $0.33.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The 200-day SMA ($0.39) acted as a strong obstacle for Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ). Though the bulls pushed the price above the resistance on several occasions, they failed to build upon the strength.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/524a9414-1eef-4b41-b539-6a20e70ac3ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down and slipped below the support at $0.38 on Feb. 9. Sellers will try to pull the price to the 50-day SMA ($0.33), which is likely to act as a strong support. If the price rebounds off the 50-day SMA with strength, it will suggest that bulls are attempting to form a higher low.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, buyers will have to overcome the zone between the 200-day SMA and $0.42 to hint at a potential trend change. That could increase the possibility of a rally above $0.44.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) plunged below the $0.09 support on Feb. 9 and reached the 50-day SMA ($0.08). This dip has pulled the RSI into the negative territory, indicating that the momentum has shifted in favor of the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/3564e418-cebf-48cd-bcb6-4e54d27bb660.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to defend the zone between the moving averages with all their might because if they fail to do that, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to the important support near $0.07. If the price rebounds off this level, the pair may consolidate between $0.07 and $0.10 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level with strength, it will indicate that the bulls are striving to flip the 200-day SMA ($0.08) into support. If they do that, the pair could start its journey back toward $0.10.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers pushed Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) above the $1.30 overhead resistance on Feb. 8 and 9 but could not sustain the breakout. This shows that bears sold the rise above $1.30.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/2b25a4ea-0a19-4066-a256-edbd6813b7b8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, a positive sign is that the bulls have not ceded much ground to the bears. This suggests that shallow dips are attracting buyers. This enhances the prospects of a rally above $1.30. If that happens, the MATIC/USDT pair could surge to $1.45 and then to $1.70.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price once again turns down from the overhead resistance, it will suggest that bears continue to fiercely guard the $1.30 level. The bears will have to sink the price below $1.16 to make way for a retest of $1.05.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-price-risks-20-correction-amid-sec-s-crackdown-on-crypto-staking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum price risks 20% correction amid SEC\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on crypto staking}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $102.50 on Feb. 8. This shows that the failure to break above the resistance may have tempted short-term traders to book profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/9991c8c7-60b8-46ab-9033-2a8aceb1f3bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to arrest the decline at the immediate support of $88 while the bears will attempt to pull the LTC/USDT pair to the 50-day SMA ($84). A deeper decline will indicate that the momentum has weakened and that could delay the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to resume the uptrend, they will have to quickly push the price back above $98. That will signal a positive sentiment, indicating that traders are buying on dips. The bulls will then again attempt to overcome the barrier at $102.50 and start the next leg of the uptrend toward $115.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to propel Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) above $7.25 may have attracted selling by short-term traders and that has pulled the price to the 200-day SMA ($6.33).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/c3cf4272-2746-4c77-9bff-0903056526c1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers will try to arrest the decline in the zone between the moving averages and make this a higher low. If they succeed, it will suggest that the DOT/USDT pair has started a bottoming formation. A break and close above $7.25 could attract further buying and open the doors for a possible rally to $10.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price plummets below the 50-day SMA ($5.59), it will suggest that bears are back in control.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $22 and reached the 200-day SMA ($17.88). Buyers are expected to defend the zone between the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/d5df31cd-3984-4048-b009-2b370cfa859e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above $22. If they manage to do that, the AVAX/USDT pair is likely to pick up momentum and rally to $30.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price rebounds off the moving averages but fails to climb above $22. That could result in a consolidation for a few days. The bears will have to sink the price below the 50-day SMA to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the authors\u8217\'20\'19 alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvZjlkOWZjMTYtM2Y4ZC00ZTU5LTg5NzMtMTA1ZGI5Yjk5OWFhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230210ej2a000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/8: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, DOT, LTC, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,744 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are facing selling on rallies but are finding support at lower levels, signaling a potential range-bound action in the near term.\par \par \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2  Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  said on Feb. 7 that the \u8220\'20\'1Cdisinflationary process, the process of getting inflation down,\u8221\'20\'1D has started but it is still in its very early stages.\par \par \uc2 He cautioned that strong data would be met with more rate hikes. Though his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bulls-stumble-at-23-4k-as-fed-s-disinflation-sparks-btc-price-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments were mixed, they triggered buying}}}\uc2  in the S&P 500 and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) on Feb. 7 as investors speculated that the Fed may soon end its campaign of rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s strong rally in January and signs of ebbing inflation seem to have turned around \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  data on Jan. 30 shows that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-takes-lion-s-share-as-institutional-inflows-hit-7-month-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional investors pumped $117 million}}}\uc2  into digital investment products. That sent the total assets under management to $28 billion, a sharp 43% increase from its November low.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/d98d104b-f88c-4ce2-a9fc-1e616c77abd6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although the sentiment seems to have turned around, bear markets rarely end without a retracement of the rise from the low. The price needs to form a higher low followed by a higher high to confirm a potential trend change.\par \par \uc2 What are the critical support levels on Bitcoin and altcoins that could arrest future declines? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin slid below $22,800 on Feb. 6 but the bulls purchased this dip. That started a rebound above $23,000 on Feb. 7 but the buyers could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/f7f136eb-7603-419f-a740-553b6e87545c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are unlikely to have it easy because the bears will try to pose a strong challenge on every rise toward $24,000. Although the upsloping moving averages suggest advantage to buyers, the negative divergence on the relative strength index (RSI) signals that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is slowing down.\par \par \uc2 Sellers are trying to trap the aggressive bulls by pulling the price below the 20-day exponential moving average ($22,568). If they manage to do that, the BTC/USDT pair may give back a part of its recent gains and dive to $21.480. Buyers are likely to defend the zone between $21,480 and the psychologically critical level of $20,000.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($1,600) on Feb. 7. The bulls tried to solidify their position by driving the price above the $1,680 resistance on Feb. 8 but they could not sustain the breakout.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/fc27980e-47d2-4680-8a69-0e3bad7d0eb1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This shows that the bears are active near the $1,680 resistance. The sellers will try to sink the pair below the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to $1,500. The sellers will have to crack this support to seize control.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up and rises above $1,700, the pair may signal the start of the next leg of the uptrend. There is a minor resistance at $1,800, but the potential of a rally to $2,000 increases if the bulls do not allow the price to dip back below $1,680.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls successfully defended the breakout level of $318 on Feb. 6, which is a positive sign as it shows that buyers are not waiting for a deeper correction to buy. The bulls will now try to push BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above $338.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/8d545aaa-d52f-42b9-bba0-ec5974f82a67.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they can pull it off, the potential for a rally to $360 improves. The bears are expected to mount a strong defense at this level but if this barrier is surmounted, the BNB/USDT pair could extend the up-move to $400.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and plummets below $318, it will signal that bears sold on rallies. That may trap the aggressive bulls and increase the risk of a fall to the 50-day simple moving average ($284).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) back above the 20-day EMA ($0.40) on Feb. 7 but are struggling to sustain the higher levels. This suggests that the bears are not ready to let bulls have their way.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/d15bdcd3-0e81-49e3-9d46-653185158d35.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to pull the XRP/USDT pair to the strong support near $0.36. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a slide below it will suggest that the pair may extend its consolidation between $0.30 and $0.42 for a few more days. Trading inside a range is usually random and volatile.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to seize control, they will have to thrust the price above the $0.42 to $0.44 resistance zone. After this zone is cleared, there is no major resistance until $0.51, hence the pair may travel this distance in a short time.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) jumped up from the immediate support at $0.38 on Feb. 7, indicating that lower levels are attracting buyers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/d0b619a9-0033-4c9a-81e0-dcc1c2ba2cff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although the risk from the negative divergence on the RSI remains, the upsloping moving averages suggest that bulls have the upper hand. There is a minor resistance at $0.41 but if this level is crossed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair may touch $0.44. The bears will again try to stall the up-move at this level.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and plunges below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bulls are tiring out. The bears will then try to sink the price to the 50-day SMA ($0.32).\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($0.09) on Feb. 7 but the shallow rise showed a lack of aggressive buying at lower levels. The price turned down on Feb. 8 and is testing the support at the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/7c1756d9-60fb-4f88-aa9c-8b14e021b189.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If this level gives way, the sellers will try to strengthen their position by pulling the DOGE/USDT pair to the 50-day SMA ($0.08). This is an important support for the bulls to defend because if it gives way, the selling could accelerate and the pair may tumble to the crucial support at $0.07.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the bulls will have to pierce the resistance zone between $0.10 and $0.11 to clear the path for a possible rally to $0.15.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) turned up from $1.17 on Feb. 6, which is a positive sign because traders did not wait for the price to touch the 20-day EMA ($1.13) before buying.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/5ec87b23-1ee5-426b-96d3-a4e015b8c26b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the RSI remains intact but the solid rebound on Feb. 7 shows strong demand at lower levels. This improves the prospects of a break above $1.30. If this level is scaled, the MATIC/USDT pair is likely to pick up momentum and surge to $1.45 and thereafter dash to $1.70.\par \par \uc2 The long wick on the Feb. 8 candlestick shows that bears are fiercely defending the $1.30 level. Sellers will now try to strengthen their position by pulling the price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-metric-which-cued-biggest-bitcoin-bull-runs-brakes-out-at-23k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC price metric which cued biggest Bitcoin bull runs brakes out at $23K}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 In an uptrend, the bulls usually buy the dip to the 20-day EMA as it offers a low-risk trading opportunity. \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($94) on Feb. 7, signaling that the uptrend remains intact.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/2548b0bb-316b-4edb-b753-bac70eb9c91d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 There is a minor hurdle at $102.50 but if that is crossed, buyers will try to propel the LTC/USDT pair to $107. This level may again act as a roadblock but if buyers do not allow the price to dip below the 20-day EMA, the prospects of a rally to $115 increase.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bears want to gain the upper hand, they will have to sink the price below the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, several stop losses may get triggered. The pair could then start a deeper correction to the 50-day SMA ($83).\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) retest of the breakout level was successfully defended by the bulls on Feb. 7. This shows that buyers are trying to flip the resistance line into support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/51ad03a6-fa79-4d3b-9958-6603f5019ce1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are offering stiff resistance near $7. But the rising 20-day EMA ($6.41) suggests that the sentiment remains positive. If buyers drive the price above $7.12, the DOT/USDT pair could travel to $8, which is likely to again act as a strong hurdle.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the 20-day EMA. That may encourage short-term traders to book profits and open the doors for a possible decline to $6 and then to the 50-day SMA ($5.52).\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($19.28) on Feb. 7, indicating that lower levels continue to attract buyers. However, the bulls are struggling to sustain the higher levels, signaling that bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/f26a9708-64f1-4598-b1cf-8ec447c34664.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The AVAX/USDT pair is stuck between the 20-day EMA on the downside and $22 on the upside. Usually, a consolidation near an overhead resistance is a positive sign as it shows that bulls are not rushing to the exit. If buyers drive the price above $22, the pair may start its journey toward $30.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price breaks back below the resistance line, it will suggest that the bulls have given up and are booking profits. The pair could then slide to the 50-day SMA ($15.61).\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvZWExODdjM2EtNmU0Yy00OGQxLTg5OTItOTdiMTQ1YmU4ZWIzLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230209ej280000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/8: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, DOT, LTC, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,744 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are facing selling on rallies but are finding support at lower levels, signaling a potential range-bound action in the near term.\par \par 