 have to crack this support to seize control.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up and rises above $1,700, the pair may signal the start of the next leg of the uptrend. There is a minor resistance at $1,800, but the potential of a rally to $2,000 increases if the bulls do not allow the price to dip back below $1,680.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls successfully defended the breakout level of $318 on Feb. 6, which is a positive sign as it shows that buyers are not waiting for a deeper correction to buy. The bulls will now try to push BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above $338.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/8d545aaa-d52f-42b9-bba0-ec5974f82a67.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they can pull it off, the potential for a rally to $360 improves. The bears are expected to mount a strong defense at this level but if this barrier is surmounted, the BNB/USDT pair could extend the up-move to $400.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and plummets below $318, it will signal that bears sold on rallies. That may trap the aggressive bulls and increase the risk of a fall to the 50-day simple moving average ($284).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) back above the 20-day EMA ($0.40) on Feb. 7 but are struggling to sustain the higher levels. This suggests that the bears are not ready to let bulls have their way.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/d15bdcd3-0e81-49e3-9d46-653185158d35.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to pull the XRP/USDT pair to the strong support near $0.36. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a slide below it will suggest that the pair may extend its consolidation between $0.30 and $0.42 for a few more days. Trading inside a range is usually random and volatile.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to seize control, they will have to thrust the price above the $0.42 to $0.44 resistance zone. After this zone is cleared, there is no major resistance until $0.51, hence the pair may travel this distance in a short time.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) jumped up from the immediate support at $0.38 on Feb. 7, indicating that lower levels are attracting buyers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/d0b619a9-0033-4c9a-81e0-dcc1c2ba2cff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although the risk from the negative divergence on the RSI remains, the upsloping moving averages suggest that bulls have the upper hand. There is a minor resistance at $0.41 but if this level is crossed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair may touch $0.44. The bears will again try to stall the up-move at this level.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and plunges below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bulls are tiring out. The bears will then try to sink the price to the 50-day SMA ($0.32).\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($0.09) on Feb. 7 but the shallow rise showed a lack of aggressive buying at lower levels. The price turned down on Feb. 8 and is testing the support at the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/7c1756d9-60fb-4f88-aa9c-8b14e021b189.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If this level gives way, the sellers will try to strengthen their position by pulling the DOGE/USDT pair to the 50-day SMA ($0.08). This is an important support for the bulls to defend because if it gives way, the selling could accelerate and the pair may tumble to the crucial support at $0.07.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the bulls will have to pierce the resistance zone between $0.10 and $0.11 to clear the path for a possible rally to $0.15.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) turned up from $1.17 on Feb. 6, which is a positive sign because traders did not wait for the price to touch the 20-day EMA ($1.13) before buying.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/5ec87b23-1ee5-426b-96d3-a4e015b8c26b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the RSI remains intact but the solid rebound on Feb. 7 shows strong demand at lower levels. This improves the prospects of a break above $1.30. If this level is scaled, the MATIC/USDT pair is likely to pick up momentum and surge to $1.45 and thereafter dash to $1.70.\par \par \uc2 The long wick on the Feb. 8 candlestick shows that bears are fiercely defending the $1.30 level. Sellers will now try to strengthen their position by pulling the price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-metric-which-cued-biggest-bitcoin-bull-runs-brakes-out-at-23k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC price metric which cued biggest Bitcoin bull runs brakes out at $23K}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 In an uptrend, the bulls usually buy the dip to the 20-day EMA as it offers a low-risk trading opportunity. \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($94) on Feb. 7, signaling that the uptrend remains intact.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/2548b0bb-316b-4edb-b753-bac70eb9c91d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 There is a minor hurdle at $102.50 but if that is crossed, buyers will try to propel the LTC/USDT pair to $107. This level may again act as a roadblock but if buyers do not allow the price to dip below the 20-day EMA, the prospects of a rally to $115 increase.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bears want to gain the upper hand, they will have to sink the price below the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, several stop losses may get triggered. The pair could then start a deeper correction to the 50-day SMA ($83).\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) retest of the breakout level was successfully defended by the bulls on Feb. 7. This shows that buyers are trying to flip the resistance line into support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/51ad03a6-fa79-4d3b-9958-6603f5019ce1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are offering stiff resistance near $7. But the rising 20-day EMA ($6.41) suggests that the sentiment remains positive. If buyers drive the price above $7.12, the DOT/USDT pair could travel to $8, which is likely to again act as a strong hurdle.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the 20-day EMA. That may encourage short-term traders to book profits and open the doors for a possible decline to $6 and then to the 50-day SMA ($5.52).\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($19.28) on Feb. 7, indicating that lower levels continue to attract buyers. However, the bulls are struggling to sustain the higher levels, signaling that bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/f26a9708-64f1-4598-b1cf-8ec447c34664.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The AVAX/USDT pair is stuck between the 20-day EMA on the downside and $22 on the upside. Usually, a consolidation near an overhead resistance is a positive sign as it shows that bulls are not rushing to the exit. If buyers drive the price above $22, the pair may start its journey toward $30.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price breaks back below the resistance line, it will suggest that the bulls have given up and are booking profits. The pair could then slide to the 50-day SMA ($15.61).\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvZWExODdjM2EtNmU0Yy00OGQxLTg5OTItOTdiMTQ1YmU4ZWIzLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230208ej28000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin takes \u8216\'20\'18lion\u8217\'20\'19s share\u8217\'20\'19 as institutional inflows hit 7-month high\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   William Suberg \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin cleans up institutional investment as inflows hit their highest since June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) rebounding 40% in January sparked the largest inflows of institutional cash since June 2022, data shows.\par \par \uc2 In its \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D report on Jan. 30, \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment and trading group \uc2 CoinShares{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://a.storyblok.com/f/155294/x/3cbf385a56/digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-30-01-23-pdf.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  $117 million heading into crypto in the last week of the month.\par \par \uc2 Institutions \u8220\'20\'1Cnot sold\u8221\'20\'1D on post-Merge Ethereum\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is still on the radar as an institutional investment opportunity.\par \par \uc2 As demonstrated by \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 latest data, it took just weeks of BTC price action recouping prior losses to spark a significant turnaround in investment habits \u8212\'20\'14 and not just in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast week\u8217\'20\'19s US bears seem to have changed their mind with US$117m inflows, including US$26m from the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  wrote in a \uc2 Twitter{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CoinSharesCo/status/1620044195862913024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thread}}}\uc2  accompanying the report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is 3x the amount from last week. Total AuM had risen to US$28bn, up 43% from their November 2022 lows.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Germany was the surprise leader, responsible for 40% of the week\u8217\'20\'19s tally, followed by Canada.\par \par \uc2 Despite altcoins rallying in line with Bitcoin, however, institutions appear mainly interested in BTC when it comes to cash.\par \par \uc2 In the words of \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cthe focus was almost entirely on Bitcoin,\u8221\'20\'1D a fact not lost on market participants eyeing a potential shift in preferences away from the Ethereum-centric decentralized finance arena.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is evidence that institutional money isn't sold on the Ethereum thesis,\u8221\'20\'1D popular \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account Pillage Capital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PillageCapital/status/1622627299731415045"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The numbers likewise belied testing times for certain altcoins, with \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  singling out Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ), Stellar ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM}}}\uc2  ) and Uniswap ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/uniswap-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI}}}\uc2  ). Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) nonetheless saw net inflows.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMulti-asset investment products saw outflows for the 9th consecutive week totaling US$6.4m, suggesting investors are preferring select investments,\u8221\'20\'1D it commented.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/a95cfaeb-a105-4a3d-ab89-11a935f525ab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Weekly Crypto Asset Flows chart. Source: \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 / \uc2 Twitter\par \par \uc2 GBTC sinks towards new record discount\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, after staging a marked comeback of its own, the largest Bitcoin institutional investment vehicle seems to be running out of steam once more.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-sees-golden-cross-which-last-hit-2-months-before-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin sees golden cross which last hit 2 months before all-time high}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Grayscale Bitcoin Trust\uc2  (GBTC) traded at a 43% discount to the Bitcoin spot price on Feb. 7, having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-holds-17k-into-fed-powell-speech-as-gbtc-jumps-to-multi-month-highs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-holds-17k-into-fed-powell-speech-as-gbtc-jumps-to-multi-month-highs}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-holds-17k-into-fed-powell-speech-as-gbtc-jumps-to-multi-month-highs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recovered to 36.2%}}}\uc2  in mid-January.\par \par \uc2 As Cointelegraph continues to report, Grayscale currently finds itself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/gbtc-elevator-to-hell-sees-bitcoin-spot-price-approach-100-premium"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 caught up in difficulties}}}\uc2  impacting parent company \uc2 Digital Currency Group\uc2  following the disintegration of \uc2 FTX\uc2  in November 2022.\par \par \uc2 However, GBTC was already struggling, with Grayscale {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/osprey-sues-grayscale-alleging-unfair-ads-and-promos-for-etf-blocked-by-sec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempting to force U.S. regulators}}}\uc2  to allow it to convert to the country\u8217\'20\'19s first Bitcoin spot price exchange-traded fund.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/ac2dc444-bb74-4c48-bb81-8c3ad28179f7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 GBTC premium vs. asset holdings vs. BTC/USD chart. Source: Coinglass\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the authors\u8217\'20\'19 alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvNmQyZWNkMDYtYzU2MS00ZTQwLTkwNmItMGJlNzc3NmRjNjJjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230207ej270005o\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Digital bank \uc2 Revolut\uc2  launches crypto staking for UK and EEA customers: Report\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Judith BannermanQuist \par \uc2 378 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Revolut\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s staking feature is expected to go live this week during its "soft testing" phase.\par \par \uc2 United Kingdom-based neo-banking platform \uc2 Revolut\uc2 , which boasts 25 million customers globally, has introduced crypto staking to its U.K. and \uc2 European Economic Area (EEA) \uc2 customers.\par \par \uc2 According to a report from London-based news agency AltFi, the staking feature is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.altfi.com/article/10372_revolut-is-launching-crypto-staking-for-25-million-users-for-dot-xtz-ada-eth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected}}}\uc2  to go live this week, allowing users to generate income on their crypto assets during its \u8220\'20\'1Csoft testing\u8221\'20\'1D phase.\par \par \uc2 At present, the staking feature is available for Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ), Tezos\u8217\'20\'19s XTX ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xtz-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XTZ}}}\uc2  ), Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), with yields ranging from 2.99% to 11.65%. However, these yields are not guaranteed.\par \par \uc2 In cryptocurrency, staking is a process where an individual holds or locks up a certain amount of a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a wallet for a certain period, typically from several days to several months. This action helps secure the network and validates transactions on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/blockchain-for-beginners/proof-of-stake-vs-proof-of-work:-differences-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proof-of-stake blockchain}}}\uc2 . In return, individuals are rewarded newly minted coins or a share of the transaction fees.\par \par \uc2 Over the past few years, \uc2 Revolut\uc2  has been incorporating cryptocurrencies into its services. In 2017, it began offering crypto trading services, which have since become a significant source of revenue for the company, particularly with the introduction of products like crypto cashback for premium users. Now, \uc2 Revolut\uc2  offers trading for nearly 100 different crypto assets and also enables its customers to make purchases using their crypto holdings.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to educate its customers on crypto and blockchain, \uc2 Revolut\uc2  has also been offering free "Learn & Earn" courses on the basics of these topics, and rewarding users who complete the program with free crypto.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/german-neobank-n26-to-launch-crypto-trading-later-this-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 German neobank N26 to launch crypto trading later this year}}}\par \par \uc2 In September 2022, Cointelegraph reported that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fca-green-lights-revolut-making-no-uk-crypto-firms-operating-under-temporary-status"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.K.\u8217\'20\'19s Financial Conduct Authority added Revolut}}}\uc2  to its list of authorized companies offering cryptocurrency products and services.\par \par \uc2 Revolut\uc2  joined 37 other firms that have been granted the green light to offer such services in the U.K. after being granted an extension to operate as a crypto asset firm with temporary registration in March 2022.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvNmUyNTgxYWItMDRlMy00MDM1LWJlNjEtMWVjNTY3YTYyNzE0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230206ej26000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin dominates as primary focus for  \highlight22\uc2 digital asset \highlight\uc2  investors: Report\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Judith BannermanQuist \par \uc2 328 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 February 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 ' report reveals investors are primarily focusing on Bitcoin, with inflows of $69 million, accounting for 90% of total flows for the week.\par \par \uc2 On Feb. 6, European cryptocurrency investment firm \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  published its \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Report,\u8221\'20\'1D which revealed that investors are showing a strong interest in \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products, with inflows totaling $76 million last week, marking the fourth consecutive week of inflows.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-02/10012b0a-53b1-4971-9fdb-1da7accabbb8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The report indicates a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the start of 2023, with year-to-date inflows now at $230 million. This growth has led to an increase in total assets under management (AUM), which now stands at $30.3 billion \u8212\'20\'14 the highest since mid-August 2022.\par \par \uc2 Investors are primarily focusing on Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), with weekly inflows of $69 million, accounting for 90% of total flows for the week. This investment growth primarily comes from the United States, Canada and Germany, with weekly inflows of $38 million, $25 million and $24 million, respectively.\par \par \uc2 However, opinions are divided over the sustainability of this growth, with short-Bitcoin inflows totaling $8.2 million over the same period. Although these inflows are relatively small compared to long-Bitcoin inflows, they have increased by 26% of total AUM over the last three weeks. Despite this, the short-Bitcoin trade has not attracted sizable interest year-to-date, with total short-Bitcoin AUM falling by 9.2%.\par \par \uc2 Altcoins also saw some minor inflows, with Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) investment products all posting modest declines. Despite the growing clarity around unstaking, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) producers only received $700,000 in inflows.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/digital-asset-investment-products-see-highest-inflows-since-july-2022-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Digital asset\b0 \highlight22  investment products see highest inflows since July 2022: Report}}}\par \par \uc2 Overall, positive inflows into \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products highlight investors\u8217\'20\'19 growing confidence in the market. Altcoin activity also suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remains diverse and constantly evolving.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjMtMDIvOWM4ODBiM2YtOTFmMi00YmU1LTkxZDYtMDZkZTU4YmM2ZmUyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230206ej26000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
