nst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMTIvNDg2YzEyNTctOGQzZi00YWQ2LTgwM2ItNjZkZjkwNzc1MDA2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020221227eicq0002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 12/26: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, DOGE,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , MATIC, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,761 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 December 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The tight range trading in Bitcoin and altcoins could break out to the upside if the S&P 500 rises above the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency markets are trading at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-exchange-withdrawals-sink-to-7-month-low-as-users-forget-ftx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record low \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as investors have largely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-community-expresses-christmas-market-sentiments-no-santa-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stayed away during the holiday season}}}\uc2 . That could be because investors are unsure about the cryptocurrencies that could lead the next bull run.\par \par \uc2 Cumberland senior research analyst Steven Goulden said in a \u8220\'20\'1CYear in Review\u8221\'20\'1D report that he expects four \u8220\'20\'1Cemerging narratives\u8221\'20\'1D to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/4-emerging-narratives-in-crypto-to-watch-for-trading-firm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lead the crypto space}}}\uc2  over the next six to 24 months. Goulden anticipates growth in nonfungible tokens, Web3 apps and games. He expects export-oriented nations to add Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) as reserve assets and if that happens, it could be a huge positive.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/26189149-d338-4e5b-b969-18e71240507d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Jared Gross, head of institutional portfolio strategy at \uc2 JPMorgan Asset Management\uc2 , holds a different view. While speaking to Bloomberg, Gross said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-is-a-nonexistent-asset-for-big-institutional-investors-jpmorgan-exec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bear market had broken the notion}}}\uc2  that Bitcoin could act as a form of digital gold or an inflation hedge. He added that large institutional investors have stayed away from the crypto sector and that approach was unlikely to change anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 Could the S&P 500 index (SPX) and the cryptocurrency sector witness a recovery in the next few days? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 SPX\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 index (SPX) turned down sharply from the downtrend line and tumbled below the 50-day simple moving average (3,885) on Dec. 16. Buyers tried to push the price back above the 50-day SMA on Dec. 21 but the bears held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/81dfaae1-045a-4ede-8e98-e5ce49b31a37.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sellers pulled the price below the immediate support of 3,795 on Dec. 22 but the long tail on the candlestick shows strong buying at lower levels. The bulls will again try to thrust the price above the moving averages and challenge the downtrend line. A break and close above the downtrend line could indicate a potential trend change.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns down from the 20-day exponential moving average (3,907), it will suggest that the bears continue to sell on rallies. The index could then drop below 3,764 and reach the next support at 3,650.\par \par \uc2 DXY\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index (DXY) has been trading below 105 for the past few days. This suggests that the bears are trying to flip the 105 level into resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/ff0dc167-31c8-4aae-8829-d1441100e243.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating advantage to bears. If the price turns down and breaks below 103.44, the selling could pick up momentum and the index could plunge to 102 and later to the psychological level of 100. The bulls may vigorously defend this level.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the bulls will have to kick the price above the 20-day EMA (105) to suggest that the selling pressure may be reducing. The index could then attempt a rally to 107 and subsequently to 108. The bears are likely to mount a strong defense at this level.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been trading in a tiny range for the past few days. This indicates that traders are not clear about the next directional move, hence they may be sitting on the sidelines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/fd0e2b23-94c5-454c-b5ac-ed11ce92be74.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This tight-range trading may not continue for long because traders thrive in a volatile market. Buyers will try to establish their supremacy by