\par\par \b \uc2 Cardano ( \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 ) And Polkadot (DOT) Recedes To The Hideaways (HDWY) In The Wake Of FTX Collapse\b0\par\par\uc2 Crypto Daily \par \uc2 526 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2022\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2022, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 The demise of FTX created unprecedented turmoil for Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and Polkadot (DOT), causing the altcoins to lose their investors to The Hideaways (HDWY). The new generation investment has been making headlines despite the dreary cryptocurrency market.\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) Movement Under Pressure\par \par \uc2 The value of Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has seen unexpected lows amid the weeklong tale of the financial discrepancy of FTX. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  has edged down 7.10% to $0.324887 in the past month, along with an 89.50% decline from its last year's peak.\par \par \uc2 2022 has not been suitable for the cryptocurrency market as compounded miseries have dented investors' sentiment. The sudden market meltdowns turned more intense after the dramatic FTX fall.\par \par \uc2 Digital assets like Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are under pressure as their utility is tied to traders' confidence in the market. Analysts now expected \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reach $0.54 in 2023, a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  prediction compared to The Hideaways (HDWY), which recently flagged up to 40x ROI next year.\par \par \uc2 In other news, Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) unveiled plans to launch a new privacy blockchain and token but still failed to support its price movement.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) Fades Price Value\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) indicates a further downtrend in its price movement, obtaining negative sentiment from the broader market. At press time, DOT has remained negative in the 30-day timeline, translating to a decline of 8.80% to $5.56.\par \par \uc2 The series of drawbacks on Polkadot (DOT) has signified the loss of positivity in the crypto space as investors exited risky assets in light of the FTX failure.\par \par \uc2 Due to the weighing \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure, Polkadot stayed behind from high price predictions for 2023, with expectations to stay at $6.72. This is farfetched from the anticipated \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  run of The Hideaways (HDWY) next year.\par \par \uc2 The Hideaways (HDWY) Rises As Favorite Token After FTX Collapse\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency values were crushed after the FTX exchange went insolvent, but The Hideaways (HDWY) popularity surged ahead, making it the most favorite presale token.\par \par \uc2 The Hideaways has been making noise as analysts projected massive returns in 2023, supported by its lot of space for growth amid a small market cap of $45.00 million. The newest venture is set to deliver exceptional benefits that even Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and Polkadot(DOT) could not provide.\par \par \uc2 Investing in the trillion-dollar luxury property market is now easy, thanks to The Hideaways (HDWY). It mints fractionalized NFTs backed by high-tier real estate properties, handpicked by experts.\par \par \uc2 The Hideaways presale is still ongoing, offered at $0.10. This trusted project has also passed audits from the German firm Solidproof, proving its reliability to investors. In addition, HDWY has established a permanent lock on the platform\u8217\'20\'19s liquidity to highlight its long-term commitment.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thehideaways.io"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.thehideaways.io}}}\par \par \uc2 Pre-Sale: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ticket.thehideaways.io/register"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://ticket.thehideaways.io/register}}}\par \par \uc2 Telegram: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/thehideawayscrypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.me/thehideawayscrypto}}}\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hdwycrypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/hdwycrypto}}}\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020221213eicd000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 12/12: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, DOGE,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , MATIC, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,787 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s CPI data and the Federal Reserve rate hike could set the stage for fireworks in the year-end price action for Bitcoin and the S&P 500.\par \par \uc2 The Consumer Price Index (CPI) data on Dec. 13 and the outcome of the Federal Reserve meeting on Dec. 14 could influence the United States stock markets and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/biggest-week-of-the-year-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cryptocurrency markets in the near term}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders are likely to play it safe and not take large directional bets until the CPI print because any nasty surprise could produce a sharp knee-jerk reaction.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/8a4aff73-ad29-4ea4-894f-4797a6b41a53.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) could fall further before it hits a bottom, but Arthur Hayes, the former CEO of crypto derivatives platform BitMEX, thinks that Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/arthur-hayes-bitcoin-bottomed-as-everyone-who-could-go-bankrupt-has-gone-bankrupt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may have passed its worst phase}}}\uc2  for this cycle.\par \par \uc2 While speaking with podcaster and independent market analyst Scott Melker, Hayes said that he believes the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest most irresponsible entities\u8221\'20\'1D have largely dumped their Bitcoin and \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty much everyone who could go bankrupt has gone bankrupt.\u8221\'20\'1D Hayes expects Bitcoin to recover sometime in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Could risky assets witness a Santa rally and end the year on a strong footing? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 SPX\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to push the S&P 500 index (SPX) above the downtrend line may have tempted short-term traders to book profits. The price turned down on Dec. 1 and broke below the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of 3,958 on Dec. 6.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/dcd048b8-f58f-479f-8364-d3dbee711837.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to flip the 20-day EMA into resistance. If they succeed, the index could witness further selling and break below the immediate support at 3,918. That could pull the price down to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of 3,847.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up and breaks above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The index could then rise to the downtrend line. A break above this level could signal a potential trend change. The index could then rally to 4,300.\par \par \uc2 DXY\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Dollar Index (DXY) has been oscillating near the critical support of 105 for the past few days. The bears pulled the price below this level on Dec. 1 but the bulls purchased the dip near 104 and started a recovery on Dec. 5.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/4f516e24-60b9-4f26-9888-3fcfca865b50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the up-move could not even reach the 20-day EMA of 106, which suggests that the bears are aggressively selling on every minor rally. The bears will try to resume the downtrend by pulling the price below 104. If this level cracks, the next stop could be 102 and then the psychological level of 100.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to avert this decline, they will have to quickly push the price back above the 20-day EMA. The index could then rise to the overhead resistance of 108.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been stuck between $16,678 and $17,424 for the past few days. This indicates that the bears are protecting the overhead resistance at $17,622 and the bulls are buying the minor dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/e401c903-dd86-408d-88f3-b0295f89eabf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Usually, tight ranges are followed by an increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it is difficult to predict the direction of the breakout. Therefore, it is better to wait for the price to break above the resistance or below the support before taking directional bets.\par \par \uc2 The advantage could shift in favor of the buyers if the price breaks and closes above the 50-day SMA of $17,911. That could clear the path for a possible rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down and plunges below $16,678, several buyers may be forced to close their positions. That could pull the BTC/Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) pair to $15,476.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been oscillating near the 20-day EMA of $1,255 for the past few days. This indicates indecision between the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/79af5adf-fe25-47c2-a25b-cfb9f97d2621.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) near the midpoint do not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. The ETH/USDT pair may trade between $1,218 and $1,309 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 50-day SMA of $1,326. That could open the doors for a possible rally to the resistance line of the descending channel.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price breaks below $1,218, the pair could fall to $1,151 and then retest the important support at $1,073.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls repeatedly failed to push and sustain BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) price above the 20-day EMA of $288 in the past few days. The bears latched on to this opportunity and are trying to pull the price lower.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/9f24cc88-90ff-4dd2-9ab3-5fd7f3a0dc80.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has dipped below 42, indicating that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 There is a minor support at $275 but if that level gives way, the BNB/USDT pair could slump to the vital support at $250. Buyers are expected to defend this level and keep the pair range-bound between $250 and $300 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above $300 to gain the upper hand. The pair could then attempt a rally to $338.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been trading below the 20-day EMA of $0.39 since Dec. 2, indicating that the bears are guarding the level with vigor. The price tumbled down to the immediate support at $0.37 on Dec. 12.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/3231a03d-651d-4071-bc22-c1328a759025.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down gradually and the RSI has slipped near 42, suggesting that bears have the edge. If the $0.37 support gives way, the selling could intensify and the XRP/USDT pair could drop to $0.33.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price rebounds off the support at $0.37. If that happens, the pair could rise to the 20-day EMA. If the price once again turns down from this resistance, the likelihood of a break below $0.37 increases but if the 20-day EMA is scaled, the pair could climb to $0.41.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down and broke below the 50-day SMA of $0.09 on Dec. 11, which suggests that the bulls may be losing their grip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/19a4af96-3da5-4fc8-9a2d-d72dd55a77f6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOGE/USDT pair could drop to $0.08 which could act as a minor support. If the price bounces off this level but fails to break above the 20-day EMA, it will enhance the prospects of a drop to the crucial support at $0.07.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, buyers will have to kick the price above the psychological level of $0.10 to gain the upper hand. The pair could then rise to $0.11. If buyers clear this hurdle, the pair could pick up momentum and rally to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.13.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-is-a-doji-candle-pattern-and-how-to-trade-with-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What is a Doji candle pattern and how to trade with it?}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has continued its downward move and is near the vital support at $0.29. Though the RSI is showing a positive divergence, the bulls have failed to drive the price above the 20-day EMA of $0.31. This suggests that the sentiment remains negative and the bears are not willing to let go of their advantage.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/0078f06d-71e4-45b1-8f25-77552bb5d0b5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks below the $0.29 support, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could start the next leg of the downtrend. The pair could then decline to the support line, which is likely to attract buyers as the price rebounded off this level on two previous occasions.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off $0.29, the bulls will try to thrust the pair above the 20-day EMA and the overhead resistance at $0.33. If they can pull it off, the pair could rise to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) slid below the 20-day EMA of $0.90 on Dec. 11 and reached the uptrend line on Dec. 12. Buyers will try to stall the pullback at this level and start a relief rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/86e2516d-8ba9-42de-8e43-ee81e3ff0c9d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will again try to catapult the MATIC/USDT pair above the overhead resistance at $0.97. If they can accomplish that, the pair could rally to $1.05 where the bears may mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price breaks below the uptrend line, the pair could drop to $0.80 and later to $0.76. That could keep the pair sandwiched between the important levels of $0.69 and $1.05 for a while longer.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the uptrend line on Dec. 7, but the bulls could not propel the price above the 20-day EMA of $5.40. This indicates that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/20f87a44-5c34-48c2-8217-980ddc1f9d1d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down and broke below the uptrend line on Dec. 11. The bears tried to sink the DOT/USDT pair below the critical support at $5 on Dec. 12 but the long tail on the candlestick shows that bulls are trying to defend the level.\par \par \uc2 If the relief rally rises above the 20-day EMA, the recovery could pick up speed and the pair could touch the 50-day SMA of $5.82. On the other hand, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the odds of a break below $5 increase. The pair could then drop toward $4.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the authors\u8217\'20\'19 alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMTIvN2ZhOTYwNzktNTRlZS00OWE1LWIxNWItYTg0YzYwZGNkNGQ2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020221213eicc0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 12/12: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, DOGE,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , MATIC, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,770 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This week's CPI data and the Federal Reserve rate hike could set the stage for fireworks in the year-end price action for Bitcoin and the S&P 500.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price index (CPI) data on Dec. 13 and the outcome of the Federal Reserve meeting on Dec. 14 could influence the United States stock markets and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/biggest-week-of-the-year-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cryptocurrency markets in the near term}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders are likely to play it safe and not take large directional bets until the CPI print because any nasty surprise could produce a sharp knee-jerk reaction.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/8a4aff73-ad29-4ea4-894f-4797a6b41a53.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) could fall further before it hits a bottom, but Arthur Hayes, the former CEO of crypto derivatives platform BitMEX, thinks that Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/arthur-hayes-bitcoin-bottomed-as-everyone-who-could-go-bankrupt-has-gone-bankrupt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may have passed its worst phase}}}\uc2  for this cycle.\par \par \uc2 While speaking with podcaster and independent market analyst Scott Melker, Hayes said that he believesthe \u8220\'20\'1Clargest most irresponsible entities\u8221\'20\'1D have largely dumped their Bitcoin and \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty much everyone who could go bankrupt has gone bankrupt.\u8221\'20\'1D Hayes expects Bitcoin to recover sometime in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Could risky assets witness a Santa rally and end the year on a strong footing? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 SPX\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to push the S&P 500 index (SPX) above the downtrend line may have tempted short-term traders to book profits. The price turned down on Dec. 1 and broke below the 20-day exponential moving average (3,958) on Dec. 6.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/dcd048b8-f58f-479f-8364-d3dbee711837.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to flip the 20-day EMA into resistance. If they succeed, the index could witness further selling and break below the immediate support at 3,918. That could pull the price down to the 50-day simple moving average (3,847).\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up and breaks above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The index could then rise to the downtrend line. A break above this level could signal a potential trend change. The index could then rally to 4,300.\par \par \uc2 DXY\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index (DXY) has been oscillating near the critical support of 105 for the past few days. The bears pulled the price below this level on Dec. 1 but the bulls purchased the dip near 104 and started a recovery on Dec. 5.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/4f516e24-60b9-4f26-9888-3fcfca865b50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the up-move could not even reach the 20-day EMA (106) which suggests that the bears are aggressively selling on every minor rally. The bears will try to resume the downtrend by pulling the price below 104. If this level cracks, the next stop could be 102 and then the psychological level of 100.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to avert this decline, they will have to quickly push the price back above the 20-day EMA. The index could then rise to the overhead resistance of 108.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been stuck between $16,678 and $17,424 for the past few days. This indicates that the bears are protecting the overhead resistance at $17,622 and the bulls are buying the minor dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/e401c903-dd86-408d-88f3-b0295f89eabf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Usually, tight ranges are followed by an increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it is difficult to predict the direction of the breakout. Therefore, it is better to wait for the price to break above the resistance or below the support before taking directional bets.\par \par \uc2 The advantage could shift in favor of the buyers if the price breaks and closes above the 50-day SMA ($17,911). That could clear the path for a possible rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down and plunges below $16,678, several buyers may be forced to close their positions. That could pull the BTC/USDT pair to $15,476.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been oscillating near the 20-day EMA ($1,255) for the past few days. This indicates indecision between the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/79af5adf-fe25-47c2-a25b-cfb9f97d2621.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) near the midpoint do not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. The ETH/USDT pair may trade between $1,218 and $1,309 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 50-day SMA ($1,326). That could open the doors for a possible rally to the resistance line of the descending channel.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price breaks below $1,218, the pair could fall to $1,151 and then retest the important support at $1,073.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls repeatedly failed to push and sustain BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) price above the 20-day EMA ($288) in the past few days. The bears latched on to this opportunity and are trying to pull the price lower.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/9f24cc88-90ff-4dd2-9ab3-5fd7f3a0dc80.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has dipped below 42, indicating that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 There is a minor support at $275 but if that level gives way, the BNB/USDT pair could slump to the vital support at $250. Buyers are expected to defend this level and keep the pair range-bound between $250 and $300 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above $300 to gain the upper hand. The pair could then attempt a rally to $338.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been trading below the 20-day EMA ($0.39) since Dec. 2, indicating that the bears are guarding the level with vigor. The price tumbled down to the immediate support at $0.37 on Dec. 12.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-12/3231a03d-651d-4071-bc22-c1328a759025.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down gradually and the RSI has slipped near 42, suggesting that bears have the edge. If the $0.37 support gives way, the selling could intensify and the XRP/USDT pair could drop to $0.33.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price rebounds off the support at $0.37. If that happens, the pair could rise to the 20-day EMA. If the price once again turns down from this resistance, the likelihood of a break below $0.37 increases but if the 20-day EMA is scaled, the pair could climb to $0.41.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USD