\highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to build upon their advantage and resume the downtrend by pulling the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair below the support near $0.30. If they do that, the pair could drop to the support line where buyers may step in and arrest the decline.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view could invalidate in the near term if the price rebounds off the support near $0.30 and rises above the 20-day EMA. The pair could then attempt a rally to the downtrend line, indicating that the bears may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/new-btc-miner-capitulation-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New BTC miner capitulation? 5 things to know in Bitcoin this week}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) soared above the psychological level of $0.10 on Nov. 27 but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels. Profit booking pulled the price back into the range on Nov. 28.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/21b5da0a-6cb6-418d-abe7-64541caa29ea.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.09) is gradually sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating that buyers have a slight edge. If the price springs up from the 20-day EMA, the bulls will try to resume the up-move by pushing the DOGE/USDT pair above $0.11. If they manage to do that, the rally could reach the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.12.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down and breaks below the moving averages, it will suggest that the break above the range may have been a bull trap. The pair could then drop to the support at $0.07.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers are struggling to push Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.88). This suggests that bears are viewing the relief rallies as a selling opportunity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/fb8959ff-7f95-4164-b15e-7ea31a52602c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The MATIC/USDT pair could again drop to the uptrend line. This level has acted as a strong support on four previous occasions, hence the bulls will again try to defend it aggressively. If the price bounces off the uptrend line, the pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($0.90).\par \par \uc2 A break above this level will suggest that the bulls are on a comeback. The pair could then rise to $0.97. On the contrary, if the price breaks below the uptrend line, the pair could drop to the important support at $0.69.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) is in a strong downtrend. Attempts by the bulls to start a recovery fizzled out at $5.53 on Nov. 24. This suggests that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/53ef573b-2820-4ffb-9bff-f17a99b54065.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears have pulled the price near the crucial support at $5. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if they fail to do that, the DOT/USDT pair could resume the downtrend. The pair could then decline to $4.06.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off $5, it will suggest demand at lower levels. Buyers will again try to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($5.57) and extend the relief rally. The pair could then rise to $6.50.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the authors\u8217\'20\'19 alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMTEvOGNjZmM5OGQtNDU1ZS00OGI3LTk2NzYtNDlhOTk4YTM1YWQ3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020221128eibs000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
